  "steps": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large pot over medium heat. Add the onion with a pinch of salt and cook for 5 to 6 minutes, stirring often, until softened and lightly golden.",
    "Stir in the garlic and ginger, then add the cumin, ground coriander, paprika, chilli powder and cayenne. Cook for 1 minute until fragrant.",
    "Mix in the tomato paste and cook for 30 seconds, then add the pumpkin, chickpeas, canned tomatoes and water. Stir well and bring to a simmer.",
    "Cover partially and cook for 20 to 25 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the pumpkin is tender and the stew has thickened.",
    "Mash a few pieces of pumpkin against the side of the pot to make the stew silkier. Stir in the lemon juice, black pepper and more salt to taste.",
    "Serve hot topped with chopped coriander.",
